A||||18||TRiAD||Emotionally Hypersensetive People, Politics and the Workplace...||||6||
Z||000000||TRiAD||07-05-2001||11:33 AM||||OK, until very recently, I was working for a "Client-Service" company under contract for a very large insurance company. Basically, I worked for "company X", but went to work everyday for "company y", and performed all the duties (and then some) of everyone working in that department, whatever company they worked for. <BR>"Company Y" employees outnumbered us "externals" about 3 to 1, but were afraid we "were taking over" the department. <P>Anyway, being a HUGE corporation, this was most definately what you'd call a "corporate atmosphere", which basically means nobody can do ANYTHING without pissing off SOMEONE. There are some people who can do ANYTHING, and others who can do NOTHING. EVERY conversation leads to someone overhearing and getting offended by what they thought they heard, but weren't intended to hear. <P>In the one year I was there (my contract was NOT renewed) i was written up TWICE for things that fit into the following categories (not twice for each, but this is the complete list)...<P>1) "Inappropriate Conversation". Someone a few aisles over "thought" they heard a teammate and I discussing something that they wer offended by. There was no explanation, and they <B>do not tell you who it was that complained</B>, so there is no defense. <BR>(I found out later the person made it up, trying to get the person they said I was speaking with in trouble because they were applying for the same position. My write up was not removed, and there was no apology. The person who made it up admitted this, and did not get into any trouble. I was very nearly fired on the spot on this one, as they have a "0 Tolerance" policy on this kind of thing. What really pissed me off, is that the person who made this up often had inappropriate conversations, and <I>she</I> stood up one day and was talking loudly about "boobies", gesturing towards her lack thereof.). <BR>2) "Not Following Procedures". There was a new procedure where out "Team Coordinator" (TC) needed to be involved in any schedule changes, before we got them approved by "Workforce Management" (WFM), that I was not aware of. My "External Manager" set down with me and a teammate to arrange a swap in schedules, and he took this change to WFM and had it approved. I assumed that since I was working with a manager, it was all cosher, plus none of the three of us knew about the new policy. My TC asked if I could involve them next time, I said OK, and then she sent an email to her manager about it anyway. It went through 3 levels of management before it got back to me, and now, it sounded like I NEVER followed procedures. i tried to explain the situation, and that a manager was involved, and that there was no problem, but it fell on deaf ears. <BR>3) "Absences". Yeah, this one sucks. Here's the background. I am 29, have been working since I was 14, and NEVER missed more than 2 days a year from work. I had not missed a SINGLE day in over 2 years. Last winter, we had a newborn in the house, and there was the who "what-is-it-flu" going around. Well, I missed a few days. Now, "Internals" have over 10 days available "off time" when they start, I had 4. I missed more than the 4 in total, but less than 7, and this was a BIG problem. I think external firms should share in the number of available days off with the client company, so everything's fair. <P>Anyway, the point is, people SUCK! They are jealous, inscrupulous, lying, cheating, wicked, shallow things, with no concern for anything other than themselves. "Corporate Atmosperes" are hornets' nests of politics and agendas, and there is no way to win. <P>However, when I'm in Customer Service positions, the people on the other side of the phone are great! Even if they're a little "slow" or whatever, I have always given 110%. I always will. That's what I do. <BR>I am not capable of doing "an average day's work", I always work harder than I have to. Example; my last 2 days on the job, I put in TWICE as many tickets as ANYONE on my team. <BR>...Maybe that's part of why they didn't want me there...<P>Now I have to find other employment (I have some computer and a LOT of customer service experience) and must make at least $40K to make the bills, and this will be hard to do. <P>I hate working for other people now, not being in charge of my own occupational destiny. I hate the feeling that other people can decide to have a personal problem with you and determine to get you booted. But I must find something NOW. Anything. <P>I have 2 kids to take care of as well. <P>Be praying for me. I'll need it.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><I>"My God shall provide all my needs, according to His riches in Glory..."<BR>"All things work for the good of those who love the Lord..."</I> I'm counting on it...<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||p4n1c||07-05-2001||11:42 AM||||I know what you mean.  I am my senior managers illegitament(sp?) son according to a rumour.  My dad got a laugh out of that one.<P>You have to watch what you say and who you say it to.  A lot of people in my department complain about stress, well if they stopped worrying about what other people are doing or sticking their noses into other peoples business and worried about themselves and their job at hand, they wouldn't be so stressed out.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4<BR>*Under Restoration*||||reg||1
